From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:01:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: tolerate vkMapMemory on already-mapped memory

Mapping memory that is already host-mapped is invalid usage, but the Mali
DDK returns the existing mapping and some layers rely on it: GameNative's
Vulkan wrapper re-maps DXVK's persistently mapped staging memory to read
BCn data for CPU transcoding. PanVK returned VK_ERROR_MEMORY_MAP_FAILED,
the wrapper got no data and those textures stayed zero (invisible sprites
in Hades). Return the existing mapping (PanVK maps the whole BO) and count
maps; unmap on the last vkUnmapMemory. Placed maps still fail.

Tested: map_test matches the DDK; Hades renders fully; PanProbe 38/38.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: match the Mali DDK when already-mapped memory is mapped again (GameNative wrapper BCn path)
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: csf-v11/091
Validation test: map_test (double map returns VK_SUCCESS + same pointer, like the DDK); Hades (DXVK) renders fully in GameNative; PanProbe 38/38
Channel: compatibility, unsafe
Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.h |  4 ++++
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c
index cf9f4c0..92130a0 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c
@@ -352,10 +352,23 @@ panvk_MapMemory2KHR(VkDevice _device, const VkMemoryMapInfoKHR *pMemoryMapInfo,
    /* From the Vulkan 1.2.194 spec:
     *
     *    "memory must not be currently host mapped"
+    *
+    * Translation layers break this rule: GameNative's Vulkan wrapper maps
+    * memory that DXVK already keeps persistently mapped, to read texture data
+    * it converts from BCn to ASTC. The Mali blob (and other vendor drivers)
+    * return the existing mapping in that case; failing it here makes the
+    * wrapper upload all-zero textures. The whole BO is always mapped, so hand
+    * back the existing mapping and count it, and only unmap on the last
+    * vkUnmapMemory.
     */
-   if (mem->addr.host)
-      return panvk_errorf(device, VK_ERROR_MEMORY_MAP_FAILED,
-                          "Memory object already mapped.");
+   if (mem->addr.host) {
+      if (pMemoryMapInfo->flags & VK_MEMORY_MAP_PLACED_BIT_EXT)
+         return panvk_errorf(device, VK_ERROR_MEMORY_MAP_FAILED,
+                             "Memory object already mapped.");
+      mem->map_count++;
+      *ppData = (char *)mem->addr.host + offset;
+      return VK_SUCCESS;
+   }
 
    void *host_addr = NULL;
    int map_flags = MAP_SHARED;
@@ -377,6 +390,7 @@ panvk_MapMemory2KHR(VkDevice _device, const VkMemoryMapInfoKHR *pMemoryMapInfo,
 
    assert(!host_addr || addr == host_addr);
    mem->addr.host = addr;
+   mem->map_count = 1;
    *ppData = (char *)addr + offset;
 
    return VK_SUCCESS;
@@ -389,6 +403,12 @@ panvk_UnmapMemory2KHR(VkDevice _device,
    VK_FROM_HANDLE(panvk_device, device, _device);
    VK_FROM_HANDLE(panvk_device_memory, mem, pMemoryUnmapInfo->memory);
 
+   if (mem->map_count > 1) {
+      mem->map_count--;
+      return VK_SUCCESS;
+   }
+   mem->map_count = 0;
+
    if (pMemoryUnmapInfo->flags & VK_MEMORY_UNMAP_RESERVE_BIT_EXT) {
       void *reserved =
          os_mmap(mem->addr.host, pan_kmod_bo_size(mem->bo), PROT_NONE,
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.h b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.h
index 6fc545b..196927e 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.h
@@ -20,6 +20,10 @@ struct panvk_device_memory {
       void *host;
    } addr;
 
+   /* Number of outstanding vkMapMemory calls on this object (see
+    * panvk_MapMemory2KHR). */
+   uint32_t map_count;
+
    struct {
       /* Don't use this pointer, it's only to have user memory dumped when
        * PANVK_DEBUG=dump. */
-- 
